Title: Build QuickJS's std/os modules (quickjs-libc) on AROS
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: The script engine (third_party/delta/QuickJSInterpreter.cpp) runs promise jobs and timers through quickjs-libc (js_std_loop, js_std_init_handlers, js_module_set_import_meta). quickjs-libc includes poll.h, dlfcn.h, termios.h, sys/wait.h, grp.h and uses poll(), signals and pthread_condattr_setclock, none of which AROS has.
Change: _GNU_SOURCE also on AROS (setenv/unsetenv are declared only then); Treat AROS like WASI/3DS where those headers and functions are excluded (process, terminal, dynamic loading and signal functions report errors); on AROS the event loop runs timers and sleeps until the next one (no file descriptor handlers), os.Worker is not built, condition variables use CLOCK_REALTIME without a clock attribute; os.platform is "aros"; std.getenviron() returns no variables (AROS has no environ array).
Scope: AROS
Upstream: candidate (the quickjs-ng project carries quickjs-libc)
Verification: mainline x86_64, pool v1-1, 2026-11-16 (see the patch series record)
Removal: when quickjs-libc supports AROS
---
